# Shared Playwright test-account credentials.
#
# Copy this file to .env.test and fill in the values:
#
#     cp .env.test.example .env.test
#
# .env.test is gitignored. Never commit real credentials, and never hardcode
# them back into a spec — the owner password was previously duplicated across
# six files, and when it was rotated both test suites silently stopped running
# anything authenticated for about a month. Among the specs that went dark was
# cross-org-isolation.spec.ts, the one written to catch multi-tenant data leaks.
# See docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-13-dead-test-credentials.md
#
# A real environment variable overrides this file, so CI can inject values
# without one existing.
#
# Which suites need which account:
#   OWNER  — most authenticated specs, both tests/ and e2e/. Org A admin.
#   STAFF  — the other side of every cross-org isolation assertion. Org B.
#   CLIENT — client-portal specs. A customer in Org B.
#
# All three are needed for the QA suite's `setup` project to pass, because
# tests/global-setup.ts authenticates all three and saves a storageState for
# each. If any one is missing, `setup` fails and every spec that depends on it
# reports "did not run".
#
# Specs that only need an API token (no browser session) can be run without the
# setup project via --no-deps, needing just the account they actually use.

QA_OWNER_EMAIL=
QA_OWNER_PASSWORD=

QA_STAFF_EMAIL=
QA_STAFF_PASSWORD=

QA_CLIENT_EMAIL=
QA_CLIENT_PASSWORD=
